       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 30 mg is three times the FDA-labeled maximum for amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses at that level raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdose can also cause prolonged vasodilatory shock. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that ceiling.\n\nCould you check which of these you meant?\n\n- **Typo:** you meant 3 mg, which isn't a standard tablet strength, or 5 mg or 10 mg once daily.\n- **Intentional:** you want to go above the labeled max for a specific reason. If so, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Your pharmacy may still want to verify it.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
